l subscription"],"standard_of_review":"discretion_and_judgment","review_standards":["discretion_and_judgment"],"case_numbers":["2008-1"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"The Session of Crossroads Community Church challenged Philadelphia Presbytery's licensing and ordination of a candidate who stated a difference concerning women and the office of deacon but agreed to follow the BCO. The SJC denied the complaint and affirmed Presbytery's judgment; a dissent argued it should have been sustained."}},{"id":"bco:17-1--case:cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md","record_id":"case:cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md","type":"Judicial case","title":"Michael Chastain v. Heritage Presbytery","year":2007,"disposition":"out_of_order","authority_weight":"high","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.html","raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md","evidence_basis":"direct_text","relevance_status":"unreviewed","occurrences":[{"id":"bco:17-1--case:cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md:occ-6ecca25c9523","url":"https://raymond-rishty.github.io/pca-ga/cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.html","repository_path":"cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md","locator":{"fragment":null,"line":397},"excerpt":"call (BCO 17-1,2). In the same way it is only through a court of the Church","sources":["case_markdown_text"],"raw_url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/raymond-rishty/pca-ga/main/cases/ga35_2007__2006-07.md"}],"reference_presentation":{"group":"review","label":null},"metadata":{"standard_of_review":"not_reached","case_numbers":["2006-7"],"body":"SJC","synopsis":"Chastain appealed Heritage Presbytery’s 2006 excommunication and deposition. The SJC held the appeal judicially out of order because Chastain had renounced PCA jurisdiction on May 8, 2006. Consequently, Presbytery’s later proceedings were moot and SJC 2005-1 remained in effect. The SJC did not reach the merits. A concurrence questioned the discipline process after renunciation; a dissent argued t